{%- comment -%}
  HIVOLT — templates/page.shipping.liquid
  ───────────────────────────────────────
  Alternate page template. In the admin: Pages → Shipping → Template suffix →
  "shipping". Renders inside layout/theme.liquid, which supplies <main>.

  Styles live in site/theme/pages.css. build-theme.py concatenates that into
  the single assets/hivolt.css that layout/theme.liquid already links, after
  theme-hivolt.css — so there is no second stylesheet to add.

  Every figure on this page is one the store has published elsewhere and can
  stand behind: free on every US order with no minimum, 8-14 business days,
  dispatched from Illinois, tracked from dispatch, continental US only.

  There is no expedited tier, no free-shipping threshold, no international rate
  card and no carrier named, because none of those exist. Where a fact is
  missing it is left out rather than filled in.

  The FAQPage JSON-LD at the foot mirrors the visible questions word for word.
  Marking up an answer that is not on the page is a structured-data violation
  and, more to the point, a lie in a machine-readable format.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign contact_url = pages.contact.url | default: '/pages/contact-us' -%}

<nav class="crumb wrap" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
  <ol>
    <li><a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">Home</a></li>
    <li aria-current="page">{{ page.title | default: 'Shipping' | escape }}</li>
  </ol>
</nav>

<section class="hero hero--doc wrap">
  <p class="mono hero__eyebrow">Shipping policy</p>
  <h1 class="hero__h">Free, tracked,<br>and slower than<br><em>you would like.</em></h1>
  <p class="hero__sub">
    Every order inside the United States ships free with no minimum to reach,
    and takes 8&ndash;14 business days. That is the entire policy. There is no
    expedited tier to upsell you and no spend threshold to unlock.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="pg wrap">
  <div class="sec__head">
    <h2 class="sec__h">The terms</h2>
    <span class="mono">No asterisks</span>
  </div>

  <div class="pg__cols">
    <div class="rte">
      <h3>Why 8&ndash;14 days and not 2</h3>
      <p>
        Orders are picked, packed and dispatched by a fulfilment partner rather
        than out of a warehouse we run ourselves. That adds a handling step
        between your order landing and the parcel moving, and the handling step
        is where the days go.
      </p>
      <p>
        We could print two-day delivery on this page. We would then miss it on
        most orders, and you would find out at the door rather than here. Quoting
        a window we can actually hit is worth more than quoting one we cannot, so
        8&ndash;14 business days is what we publish and what we plan against. If
        that is too slow for what you need it for, this is the page that tells
        you so before you pay rather than after.
      </p>

      <h3>What business days means</h3>
      <p>
        Monday to Friday, not counting public holidays. An order placed on a
        Friday evening starts its count the following week.
      </p>

      <h3>Tracking</h3>
      <p>
        Every order is tracked from dispatch. The tracking number is emailed to
        the address on the order as soon as the parcel is handed over, and it is
        the same number you can hand to the carrier if something goes wrong. If
        you have not received it, write to us and we will send it again.
      </p>

      <h3>Where we ship</h3>
      <p>
        The continental United States only. We do not ship internationally, and
        we would rather say no here than take an order we cannot deliver
        properly. If that changes, it will be announced on this page first.
      </p>
    </div>

    <aside class="pg__aside">
      <p class="mono pg__aside-h">Shipping, as data</p>
      <div class="sheet">
        <div class="sheet__row">
          <span class="sheet__k">Cost</span>
          <span class="sheet__v"><em>Free</em></span>
        </div>
        <div class="sheet__row">
          <span class="sheet__k">Order minimum</span>
          <span class="sheet__v">None</span>
        </div>
        <div class="sheet__row">
          <span class="sheet__k">Delivery window</span>
          <span class="sheet__v">8&ndash;14 business days</span>
        </div>
        <div class="sheet__row">
          <span class="sheet__k">Dispatched from</span>
          <span class="sheet__v">Illinois, USA</span>
        </div>
        <div class="sheet__row">
          <span class="sheet__k">Tracking</span>
          <span class="sheet__v">From dispatch</span>
        </div>
        <div class="sheet__row">
          <span class="sheet__k">Ships to</span>
          <span class="sheet__v">Continental US</span>
        </div>
        <div class="sheet__row">
          <span class="sheet__k">International</span>
          <span class="sheet__v">Not available</span>
        </div>
        <div class="sheet__row">
          <span class="sheet__k">Expedited option</span>
          <span class="sheet__v">None</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="sheet__src">
        Business days are Monday to Friday, excluding public holidays.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>

{%- if page.content != blank -%}
  <section class="pg wrap">
    <div class="rte">
      {{ page.content }}
    </div>
  </section>
{%- endif -%}

<!-- ── FAQ: mirrored exactly by the JSON-LD below ──────────── -->
<section class="faq">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="faq__h">Shipping questions</h2>
    <div class="faq__list">
      <details>
        <summary>How much is shipping?</summary>
        <p class="faq__a">Nothing. Every order inside the United States ships free,
          with no minimum spend and no threshold to unlock.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How long does delivery take?</summary>
        <p class="faq__a">8&ndash;14 business days. Business days are Monday to
          Friday, excluding public holidays.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Why does it take 8&ndash;14 days?</summary>
        <p class="faq__a">Orders are dispatched by a fulfilment partner rather than
          from a warehouse we run ourselves, and that handling step is where the
          days go. We would rather quote a window we can hit than a shorter one we
          would miss on most orders.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Where does my order ship from?</summary>
        <p class="faq__a">A fulfilment facility in Illinois.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Do I get tracking?</summary>
        <p class="faq__a">Yes. Every order is tracked from dispatch and the tracking
          number is emailed to the address on the order.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Do you ship outside the United States?</summary>
        <p class="faq__a">No. Continental United States only. If that changes it
          will be announced on this page first.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {"@type":"Question","name":"How much is shipping?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Nothing. Every order inside the United States ships free, with no minimum spend and no threshold to unlock."}},
    {"@type":"Question","name":"How long does delivery take?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"8-14 business days. Business days are Monday to Friday, excluding public holidays."}},
    {"@type":"Question","name":"Why does it take 8-14 days?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Orders are dispatched by a fulfilment partner rather than from a warehouse we run ourselves, and that handling step is where the days go. We would rather quote a window we can hit than a shorter one we would miss on most orders."}},
    {"@type":"Question","name":"Where does my order ship from?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A fulfilment facility in Illinois."}},
    {"@type":"Question","name":"Do I get tracking?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Every order is tracked from dispatch and the tracking number is emailed to the address on the order."}},
    {"@type":"Question","name":"Do you ship outside the United States?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. HIVOLT ships to the continental United States only."}}
  ]
}
</script>

<!-- ── questions ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="pg__qw wrap">
  <div class="pg__q">
    <p class="pg__q-t">
      <span class="mono">Questions?</span>
      If your question about an order or a delivery is not answered above, ask us
      directly. Replies within one business day.
    </p>
    <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="{{ contact_url }}">Contact us</a>
  </div>
</section>
